.TP
\f[CR]\-\-vsplit\f[R]
Open the supplied file(s) in a \f[B]vertical\f[R] split view.
.TP
\f[CR]\-\-hsplit\f[R]
Open the supplied file(s) in a \f[B]horizontal\f[R] split view.
.TP
\f[CR]\-s SESSION_NAME\f[R], \f[CR]\-\-session SESSION_NAME\f[R]
Load a named session on startup.
See \f[B]lektra\-config(5)\f[R] for how sessions are stored.
.TP
\f[CR]\-c CONFIG_PATH\f[R], \f[CR]\-\-config CONFIG_PATH\f[R]
Path to an alternative \f[CR]config.toml\f[R] or \f[CR]init.lua\f[R]
file, selected by extension.
Only that file is loaded: a \f[CR].toml\f[R] path loads just that
configuration (compiled\-in defaults otherwise, no \f[CR]init.lua\f[R]),
a \f[CR].lua\f[R] path loads just that script (no
\f[CR]config.toml\f[R]).
See \f[B]lektra\-config(5)\f[R] for the full configuration reference.
.TP
\f[CR]\-\-about\f[R]
Show the \f[I]About Lektra\f[R] dialog and exit.
.TP
\f[CR]\-\-tutorial\f[R]
Open with the built\-in tutorial file loaded.
.TP
\f[CR]\-n\f[R], \f[CR]\-\-new\-window\f[R]
Open the file(s) in a separate window, even if single\-instance mode is
on.
.TP
\f[CR]\-\-single\-instance\f[R]
Force single\-instance mode for this invocation: if lektra is already
running, the files are opened in that instance.
.TP
\f[CR]\-\-socket SOCKET_PATH\f[R]
Listen on the given socket path instead of the default IPC socket.
.TP
\f[CR]\-\-foreground\f[R]
Do \f[B]not\f[R] detach from the terminal.
The process stays in the foreground, which is useful for capturing
stdout/stderr or running under a debugger.
.TP
\f[CR]\-\-synctex\-forward {pdf\-file}#{src\-file}:{line}:{col}\f[R]
Perform a SyncTeX forward search, jumping to the location in the PDF
that corresponds to the given source position.
.RS
\f[B]Only available when lektra is compiled with synctex support.\f[R]
.RE
.TP
\f[CR]\-\-command\f[R]
Specify one or more valid lektra commands (see
\f[CR]\-\-list\-commands\f[R]) chained together by ; (semicolon).
The commands are executed left to right.
.SS STARTUP BEHAVIOUR
On launch, lektra performs a \f[B]double\-fork\f[R] so that the
grandchild process is fully detached from the calling TTY and the parent
shell returns immediately.
The re\-executed grandchild always receives the implicit
\f[CR]\-\-foreground\f[R] flag, so the detach logic runs exactly once.
.PP
Pass \f[CR]\-\-foreground\f[R] explicitly to skip the fork entirely \(em
useful when running lektra from a compositor script, systemd user unit,
or test harness.
.SS FILES
.TP
\f[CR]$XDG_CONFIG_HOME/lektra/config.toml\f[R]
Default user configuration file.
See \f[B]lektra\-config(5)\f[R].
.TP
\f[CR]$XDG_CONFIG_HOME/lektra/init.lua\f[R]
Optional Lua script, run at startup for scripting and options.
.TP
\f[CR]$XDG_DATA_HOME/lektra/sessions/\f[R]
Directory where named sessions are persisted.
.TP
\f[CR]$XDG_DATA_HOME/lektra/bookmarks.json\f[R]
Saved bookmarks.
.TP
\f[CR]share/lektra/lua/\f[R], \f[CR]share/lektra/lektra\-config.schema.json\f[R]
Installed Lua type stubs and the JSON Schema for \f[CR]config.toml\f[R],
for completion in editors and language servers.
.SS EXAMPLES
Open a single file:
.IP
.EX
lektra document.pdf
.EE
.PP
Open at page 42:
.IP
.EX
lektra \-p 42 document.pdf
.EE
.PP
Open two files side\-by\-side:
.IP
.EX
lektra \-\-vsplit file1.pdf file2.pdf
.EE
.PP
Open with a custom config and a specific layout:
.IP
.EX
lektra \-\-config \(ti/dotfiles/lektra.toml \-\-layout book thesis.pdf
.EE
.PP
Run in the foreground (e.g.\ to see log output):
.IP
.EX
lektra \-\-foreground document.pdf
.EE
.PP
Load a saved session:
.IP
.EX
lektra \-\-session research
.EE
.PP
Open a file in a new window, even if lektra is already running:
.IP
.EX
lektra \-\-new\-window document.pdf
.EE
.PP
Open files in a grid layout:
.IP
.EX
lektra \-\-layout grid page1.png page2.png page3.png page4.png
.EE
.PP
Use a Lua script as the only configuration:
.IP
.EX
lektra \-\-config \(ti/dotfiles/init.lua document.pdf
.EE
.PP
Jump to a position in a PDF from a LaTeX source (SyncTeX):
.IP
.EX
lektra \-\-synctex\-forward \(dqpaper.pdf#paper.tex:120:1\(dq
.EE
.PP
Run commands after opening a file
.IP
.EX
lektra \-\-command \(dqfullscreen; search hello; page_goto 4\(dq document.pdf
.EE
